  "decision_conditions": [
    "The development hereby permitted shall be commenced before the expiration of three years from the date of this permission.<br>",
    null,
    "Prior to first use of the care home,&nbsp;details demonstrating that the approved development has achieved Secured by Design certification shall be submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority, in consultation with the Metropolitan Police. All security measures implemented as part of the certification shall be permanently retained thereafter.",
    "a) Prior to first use of the care home, details including the design and location of all cycle parking spaces shall be submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning authority. All cycle storage should be designed and laid out in accordance with the guidance contained in the London Cycling Design Standards. (b)&nbsp; The approved details shall be implemented prior to first use of the development and thereafter permanently retained for the lifetime of the development.&nbsp;",
    "2.&nbsp;Care Home Use and CapacityNotwithstanding the provisions of the Town and Country Planning (Use Classes) Order 1987 (as amended) (or any order revoking and re‑enacting that Order with or without modification) or the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development (England) Order 2015 (as amended) (or any order revoking and re‑enacting that Order with or without modification), the premises shall be used only as a children’s care home (Use Class C2) and for no other purpose within that Class. The care home shall accommodate no more than 1 child, 2 carers, and 1 manager at any one time.",
    "Operational Management Plana) Prior to first use of the care home, an Operational Management Plan must be submitted and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority. It must clearly outline but not be limited to how the care home will operate,&nbsp; noise management measures and include a&nbsp;commitment to prioritise referrals from the London Borough of Barking and Dagenham.b)&nbsp;The children’s home shall operate in accordance with the approved Operational Management Plan.The applicant shall notify the Council of any forthcoming placements and provide confirmation of referral origin upon request.",
    "&lt;p&gt;The development hereby approved shall only be carried out in accordance with the following approved plans and documents:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Proposed Ground and First Floor Plans (dated: 16/10/2025)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Community facility Needs Statement (received: 18/11/2025)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Planning Statement (dated: October 2025)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Site Location Plan (dated: 03/11/2024)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Block Plan (dated: 03/11/2024)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;p&gt;No other drawings or documents apply.&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
